WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.677
If switches 2, 3, 4 and 7 are on, how is that 0111 0010?

2
00:00:07.027 --> 00:00:12.795
Every switch has two labels. Its number, counted from the left, starting at 1.

3
00:00:12.795 --> 00:00:15.161
That number is the field number.

4
00:00:15.511 --> 00:00:21.806
And its worth: 8, 4, 2, 1, in each half. The worth is only for writing the hex.

5
00:00:22.156 --> 00:00:33.324
One bit per switch, left to right. 1 off: 0. 2, 3, 4 on: 111. 5, 6 off: 00. 7

6
00:00:33.324 --> 00:00:35.645
on: 1. 8 off: 0.

7
00:00:35.995 --> 00:00:43.057
Left half 0111: 0×8 + 1×4 + 1×2 + 1×1 = 7.

8
00:00:43.407 --> 00:00:48.251
Right half 0010: only the 2 is on = 2.

9
00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:51.289
Side by side: hex 72.

10
00:00:51.639 --> 00:00:56.758
It felt backwards because in the bits note you counted the worth from the right.

11
00:00:56.758 --> 00:01:00.725
The switch number counts from the left. Both are true at once.

12
00:01:01.075 --> 00:01:08.512
Your turn. Row 2 holds fields 9 to 16. Fields 11 and 14 are on. Pause and work

13
00:01:08.512 --> 00:01:09.751
out the byte.

14
00:01:12.751 --> 00:01:23.835
Field 11 is the 3rd switch, field 14 the 6th. 0010 0100. 2 and 4: hex 24.
